{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 12, :comments ["<b>And it shall be when the Egyptians see you, and they shall kill me but you they shall keep alive.</b> For they are warned against a married woman — attached to his wife and not to another's wife. And if you ask: are they not likewise warned against bloodshed, from when they emerged from the ark? One may answer that they are steeped in sexual immorality, and they will sin abundantly in murder together with adultery. Another interpretation: it is preferable for them to sin once in bloodshed than to be sinning constantly with another's wife. Another interpretation: <b>and they shall kill me</b> — lest I cry out to the king over the fact that they took you."], :book :genesis, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 12, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T15:04:00.584879010Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}